  message: "OWNER, in session 2026-11-24: 'we will also need to tackle WI-jizos-tajib with similar priority' (similar to the variable-scope change, INV-zabud; both ahead of the fifteen bump items). WIDER THAN FILED, grep on dev 7f814445a: (A) git pushes with the token inside -c credential.helper=...: scripts/auto-pr lines 1057, 1150, 1162, 1786, 2381, 2693; scripts/contribute 237; scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh 505; hypergumbo_tracker/sync.py 1696 (one helper string, used at 1704, 1788, 1899). scripts/tag-release has NO such site (the item said it did: its matches are comments about gh auth). (B) NOT in the item: curl is given the token as an argument, -H 'Authorization: token ...', on every forge API call: scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh 180 (the central wrapper) and 1141, 1166, 1195, 1225, 1284; scripts/ci-debug 781; scripts/lib/github-api.sh 157 (Woodpecker bearer); scripts/release 124. (C) the repo prints process lists itself: .agent/hooks/_shared/stop_logic.sh 243 runs pgrep -af on a watched pattern, and its output goes into hook guidance. In-process users (urllib in sync.py, stop_hook.py, on_transcript_change.py) and GH_TOKEN=... gh (environment) do not put the token on a command line. PLAN: git: the helper reads two environment variables set for that one git process, so argv holds names only; curl: the header goes through a file descriptor (-H @file), never argv; one test that runs each wrapper against a fake git / curl that records its own argv and asserts the token is absent."  # d2df
