  message: "Fixed in PR #2384 (e69760141 on dev). git: the credential helper names two environment variables set for that one git process (scripts/lib/secret-args.sh git_with_token: auto-pr 6 sites, contribute 1, forgejo-api.sh 1; hypergumbo_tracker/sync.py _CREDENTIAL_HELPER + env on its 3 pushes). curl: secret headers go on standard input, -H @- (curl_with_secret_headers: forgejo-api.sh central wrapper + 5, ci-debug, github-api.sh _wp_curl with its 3 secret headers, release). EVIDENCE: (1) behaviour, re-run on merged dev 5db33d7f6: tests/test_token_not_on_command_line.py, 12 passed: stand-ins for git and curl record their own arguments, the token is absent from them and still arrives (helper answers with it; header received); a mutation putting one header back as an argument failed 2 tests before the commit. (2) the real git answered 'credential fill' through the helper, and the real curl delivered stdin headers to a listener on 127.0.0.1. (3) the PR was itself sent by the changed auto-pr: branch push and API PR-create both succeeded on the first try (.git/autopr-detached.log), then CI polling and merge. (4) grep on dev: no credential.helper=\"...\" with a value left in auto-pr, contribute or forgejo-api.sh. NOT COVERED: the token that reached a transcript on 2026-11-24 is NOT rotated (owner's); the repo's archive scrubber redacts it from the repo's transcript copy at session end (dry run: 2 occurrences), not from ~/.claude; the next tracker auto-sync is the first real use of the Python path (this note may trigger it)."  # f73e
